    "body": "Hmm.\r\n\r\nSo a reserved environment doesn't have a global object. So we'd need some additional branching in encoding-parse a URL (and we'd also need to allow passing in an environment, or alternatively we pass in a dummy document?). (The current text might be slightly wrong there, using relevant global object instead of just global object.)\r\n\r\nIf we know for sure the document is not parsed but is a document I think it works, as the default encoding is UTF-8.",
